# Vietnamese weekdays are ORDINAL-NUMBERED: thứ ("rank") plus a number,
# counting from Sunday, which is named instead (chủ nhật, "lord's day").
# Monday is therefore "rank two".  CLDR spells the same construction two
# ways -- wide "Thứ Hai", abbreviated "Thứ 2" -- and both are listed,
# because they are one construction in two spellings, not a name and an
# abbreviation of it.
# Source: Unicode CLDR, cldr-json cldr-dates-full/main/vi/ca-gregorian.json.
thứ hai
thứ 2
